[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m #### Step 4: Analyze perturbation **D**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - **Perturb(D)**: D is perturbed → D is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - Now we look at the descendants of D in the graph.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - D has no outgoing edges, so no descendants.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - Thus, the only nodes that are 1 are those that are descendants of D (i.e., none).
