[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m ### 2. **Perturb(C) → A:0, B:0, C:0, D:0**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - **C is perturbed** → C is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - **D is not perturbed**, so D is 1 if it is a downstream descendant of a perturbed node. But C is not a downstream descendant of any node (no edges from C), so D is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - **A is not perturbed**, so A is 1 if it is a downstream descendant of a perturbed node. But A has no incoming edges, so A is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m So the final node states:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - A: 0 (not a descendant of C)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - B: 0 (not a descendant of C)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - C: 0 (perturbed)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - D: 0 (not a descendant of C)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m This matches the perturbation observation: **Perturb(C) → A:0, B:0, C:0, D:0**
