[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m #### 2. Perturb(B) -> A:0, B:0, C:0, D:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - B is perturbed (so it is 0).
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - The graph has an edge `C->B`, so C is upstream of B. But B is perturbed, so B is 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - B has no outgoing edges, so no downstream descendants.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - Therefore, the output is: A:0, B:0, C:0, D:0 — **consistent**.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m #### 3. Perturb(C) -> A:1, B:1, C:0, D:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - C is perturbed (so it is 0).
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - The graph has an edge `C->B`, so C is upstream of B. Hence, B is a downstream descendant of C.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - Therefore, B is 1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - C has no outgoing edges, so no downstream descendants.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - Therefore, the output is: A:1, B:1, C:0, D:0 — **consistent**.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
