[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m ### Step 1: Understand the semantics of perturbation
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - A node is 0 if it is not perturbed.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - A node is 1 if it is a downstream descendant of the perturbed node.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - All other nodes are 0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m So for each perturbation, we must check:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - What is the perturbed node (e.g., B, C, or D)?
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - What is the perturbed node's value (0)?
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - What are the downstream descendants of the perturbed node?
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - Assign values accordingly.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m Let's go through each perturbation one by one.
