[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - A node is **0** if it is **not** a downstream descendant of the perturbed node.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - A node is **1** if it is a downstream descendant of the perturbed node.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m - All other nodes are **0**.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m So, for each perturbation, we need to:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 1. Find the perturbed node (e.g., B)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 2. Find all downstream descendants of B in the graph
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2391518)[0m 3. Assign 1 to those descendants, 0 otherwise.
